1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,081
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:04,081 --> 00:00:09,260
It's a conversation about the new semester.

3
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: New Semester and Summer Vacation Memories

4
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:16,699
Oh, good morning, Ken!

5
00:00:16,722 --> 00:00:20,989
Good morning, Sato!

6
00:00:21,012 --> 00:00:24,445
Long time no see!

7
00:00:24,468 --> 00:00:29,251
Yeah, it's been a while.

8
00:00:29,275 --> 00:00:34,142
Today marks the start of September and the new semester, huh?

9
00:00:34,165 --> 00:00:37,232
Yeah, it does.

10
00:00:37,255 --> 00:00:41,688
How was your summer break?

11
00:00:41,711 --> 00:00:44,790
Did you have a good time?

12
00:00:44,813 --> 00:00:53,047
Yes! I went on a trip to Hokkaido with friends, and it was amazing.

13
00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:56,246
That sounds great!

14
00:00:56,269 --> 00:01:00,382
How was Hokkaido?

15
00:01:00,405 --> 00:01:06,676
It was cool and the weather was perfect.

16
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:12,087
Did you try any delicious food there?

17
00:01:12,111 --> 00:01:18,611
Yes! I had famous ramen and some delicious fish.

18
00:01:18,634 --> 00:01:21,700
That sounds great!

19
00:01:21,723 --> 00:01:27,041
I’d love to visit Hokkaido someday too.

20
00:01:27,065 --> 00:01:31,169
It’s a wonderful place.

21
00:01:31,193 --> 00:01:34,827
You should definitely go!

22
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:39,360
Yeah, I’ll try to go sometime!

23
00:01:39,383 --> 00:01:44,416
What did you do during summer break, Ken?

24
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:50,673
I went back to my hometown and relaxed with my family.

25
00:01:50,696 --> 00:01:56,935
I see. You must’ve had a good rest.

26
00:01:56,959 --> 00:02:05,325
Yeah, but I also worked a lot at a café in late August.

27
00:02:05,348 --> 00:02:09,223
Wow, you worked hard at your part-time job!

28
00:02:09,247 --> 00:02:12,880
Didn’t you get tired?

29
00:02:12,903 --> 00:02:20,537
A little, but I managed to save up a lot of money, so it was worth it.

30
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:23,896
That’s impressive!

31
00:02:23,919 --> 00:02:30,452
By the way, have you bought your new semester textbooks yet?

32
00:02:30,475 --> 00:02:34,709
No, not yet.

33
00:02:34,732 --> 00:02:38,698
I’m going to buy mine this afternoon.

34
00:02:38,721 --> 00:02:43,555
Me neither.

35
00:02:43,578 --> 00:02:48,644
Want to go together after class this afternoon?

36
00:02:48,667 --> 00:02:53,501
Yes, let’s go together!

37
00:02:53,524 --> 00:02:58,100
What time does class end today?

38
00:02:58,123 --> 00:03:02,390
It ends at 3:30.

39
00:03:02,413 --> 00:03:09,523
Then let’s meet at 3:45 in front of the bookstore.

40
00:03:09,546 --> 00:03:12,380
Got it.

41
00:03:12,403 --> 00:03:15,948
3:45, right?

42
00:03:15,972 --> 00:03:23,238
Let’s buy our new textbooks and do our best this semester together!

43
00:03:23,261 --> 00:03:27,561
Yeah, let’s do our best together!

44
00:03:27,584 --> 00:03:32,018
See you later!

45
00:03:32,041 --> 00:03:35,708
See you later!

46
00:03:35,731 --> 00:03:44,740
You can download today’s script from the description and top comments. Please leave a comment before downloading!

47
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,240
Scene 2: Choosing Classes – A Consultation

48
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:50,374
Hi, Mai!

49
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:55,830
Are you checking your schedule on the computer?

50
00:03:55,853 --> 00:04:00,553
Oh, hi Suzuki!

51
00:04:00,576 --> 00:04:06,055
Yeah, I’m looking up my fall semester classes.

52
00:04:06,078 --> 00:04:12,018
Have you decided which classes to take yet?

53
00:04:12,042 --> 00:04:16,909
No, I haven’t decided yet.

54
00:04:16,932 --> 00:04:20,509
I’m a little torn.

55
00:04:20,532 --> 00:04:24,798
What kind of classes do you want to take?

56
00:04:24,821 --> 00:04:31,499
I want to take a Japanese culture class and a conversation class.

57
00:04:31,523 --> 00:04:38,956
There’s a Japanese culture class on Monday during the third period.

58
00:04:38,979 --> 00:04:43,079
What’s that class like?

59
00:04:43,102 --> 00:04:46,292
Is it interesting?

60
00:04:46,316 --> 00:04:51,549
Yes, it’s really fun!

61
00:04:51,572 --> 00:04:56,039
The teacher is also really kind.

62
00:04:56,062 --> 00:05:00,054
Is the test difficult?

63
00:05:00,077 --> 00:05:04,510
No, there’s no test.

64
00:05:04,534 --> 00:05:09,009
You just write a short report.

65
00:05:09,032 --> 00:05:11,983
Oh, really?!

66
00:05:12,006 --> 00:05:16,599
If that’s the case, I can take it too!

67
00:05:16,623 --> 00:05:21,323
Suzuki, are you taking that class too?

68
00:05:21,346 --> 00:05:28,618
Yeah, I’m taking it Monday during the third period too.

69
00:05:28,641 --> 00:05:31,779
Let’s take it together!

70
00:05:31,803 --> 00:05:34,503
Great!

71
00:05:34,526 --> 00:05:39,106
I’m happy I’ll have a friend to take it with.

72
00:05:39,129 --> 00:05:43,163
Me too.

73
00:05:43,187 --> 00:05:48,338
What classes do you want to take on Tuesday?

74
00:05:48,361 --> 00:05:55,594
I want to take a Japanese presentation class during the first period on Tuesday.

75
00:05:55,617 --> 00:06:01,185
What time does the first-period class start?

76
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:05,483
It starts at 9 AM.

77
00:06:05,507 --> 00:06:11,451
How long does it take to get from Mai’s house to the university?

78
00:06:11,475 --> 00:06:19,008
It takes an hour by train, so you’ll have to wake up early.

79
00:06:19,031 --> 00:06:23,414
That sounds tough.

80
00:06:23,438 --> 00:06:30,150
But you’ll get lots of practice speaking Japanese!

81
00:06:30,173 --> 00:06:32,957
I see.

82
00:06:32,981 --> 00:06:39,814
Since I want to improve my Japanese, I’ll make sure to wake up early.

83
00:06:39,837 --> 00:06:43,415
That’s amazing!

84
00:06:43,439 --> 00:06:49,145
Do you have any classes Thursday afternoon?

85
00:06:49,169 --> 00:06:54,802
No, I don’t have any classes Thursday afternoon.

86
00:06:54,825 --> 00:06:58,701
I’ll study at the library.

87
00:06:58,725 --> 00:07:01,825
That sounds great!

88
00:07:01,848 --> 00:07:07,584
Taking too many classes every day can be exhausting.

89
00:07:07,608 --> 00:07:09,783
Yeah.

90
00:07:09,806 --> 00:07:15,873
This semester, I’ll do my best at my own pace without pushing myself too hard.

91
00:07:15,896 --> 00:07:19,864
That’s the best approach.

92
00:07:19,888 --> 00:07:24,884
Let’s register on the computer today.

93
00:07:24,907 --> 00:07:27,623
Yeah.

94
00:07:27,646 --> 00:07:31,346
I’ll register right away.

95
00:07:31,369 --> 00:07:37,243
Suzuki, thank you for your advice!

96
00:07:37,267 --> 00:07:41,133
You’re welcome!

97
00:07:41,156 --> 00:07:46,256
See you in class on Monday!

98
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:48,746
Yeah.

99
00:07:48,769 --> 00:07:52,124
See you Monday!

100
00:07:52,148 --> 00:07:59,253
Check out the link in the description and top comment for a site to review today’s lesson! *Note: Links may be removed without notice.

101
00:07:59,253 --> 00:08:00,753
Scene 3: How to Save Money on Textbooks

102
00:08:00,753 --> 00:08:05,069
Hello, Takahashi-senpai!

103
00:08:05,092 --> 00:08:10,264
Did you come to buy textbooks too, senpai?

104
00:08:10,287 --> 00:08:14,720
Oh, Rin! Hello.

105
00:08:14,743 --> 00:08:21,410
Yeah, I came to buy the books for the fall semester classes.

106
00:08:21,433 --> 00:08:29,666
I’m looking at the textbook list too, but buying everything is so expensive.

107
00:08:29,689 --> 00:08:35,074
College textbooks really are pricey, huh?

108
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:40,131
How much will it all cost?

109
00:08:40,154 --> 00:08:46,100
Around 15,000 yen in total.

110
00:08:46,124 --> 00:08:51,122
That’s expensive!

111
00:08:51,145 --> 00:08:57,414
You don’t have to buy all new books, you know.

112
00:08:57,438 --> 00:09:00,971
Wait, really?

113
00:09:00,994 --> 00:09:05,110
How can I make it cheaper?

114
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:10,885
First, did you check the university library?

115
00:09:10,909 --> 00:09:15,342
No, I haven’t gone yet.

116
00:09:15,365 --> 00:09:20,332
Does the library have textbooks?

117
00:09:20,355 --> 00:09:23,121
Yeah.

118
00:09:23,144 --> 00:09:29,462
They have the books for your classes, so you can read them anytime.

119
00:09:29,486 --> 00:09:32,365
I see.

120
00:09:32,388 --> 00:09:37,088
Can I borrow them to take home?

121
00:09:37,111 --> 00:09:44,411
You can’t borrow them, but you can make copies inside the library.

122
00:09:44,434 --> 00:09:47,334
I see.

123
00:09:47,357 --> 00:09:52,076
Studying at the library would be a good idea.

124
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:55,008
Yeah, it does.

125
00:09:55,031 --> 00:10:01,098
Another option is to ask a senior student for theirs.

126
00:10:01,121 --> 00:10:04,489
From a senior?

127
00:10:04,512 --> 00:10:07,212
Yeah.

128
00:10:07,236 --> 00:10:14,502
Actually, I have the economics textbook that Rin is taking.

129
00:10:14,525 --> 00:10:18,064
I won’t use it anymore.

130
00:10:18,088 --> 00:10:21,921
Wait, really?!

131
00:10:21,944 --> 00:10:26,081
Can I take that book?

132
00:10:26,104 --> 00:10:29,882
Of course!

133
00:10:29,906 --> 00:10:36,446
I wrote some notes in it, but if that’s okay, you can have it.

134
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:40,969
Notes are fine with me!

135
00:10:40,992 --> 00:10:44,138
That helps a lot.

136
00:10:44,161 --> 00:10:49,028
I’ll bring it to campus tomorrow.

137
00:10:49,051 --> 00:10:51,751
Thank you so much!

138
00:10:51,774 --> 00:10:56,717
What about the other English books?

139
00:10:56,741 --> 00:11:03,774
Why not look for used copies online for the English books?

140
00:11:03,797 --> 00:11:07,631
Used books, huh?

141
00:11:07,655 --> 00:11:12,588
Can you buy them for half the price?

142
00:11:12,611 --> 00:11:15,388
Yeah.

143
00:11:15,411 --> 00:11:19,711
You can get them much cheaper.

144
00:11:19,734 --> 00:11:25,644
But make sure it’s the same edition before you buy.

145
00:11:25,668 --> 00:11:28,501
Got it.

146
00:11:28,524 --> 00:11:33,791
I’ll double-check the title and year.

147
00:11:33,814 --> 00:11:40,320
This way, you won’t spend much on textbooks.

148
00:11:40,343 --> 00:11:42,977
Yeah.

149
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,866
It’ll be around 5,000 yen.

150
00:11:46,889 --> 00:11:52,323
Thanks for your help, Senpai!

151
00:11:52,346 --> 00:11:56,979
I’m glad I could help.

152
00:11:57,002 --> 00:12:01,702
Good luck with your studies this semester!

153
00:12:01,725 --> 00:12:04,425
Yeah.

154
00:12:04,448 --> 00:12:08,192
I’ll do my best!

155
00:12:08,215 --> 00:12:11,982
See you tomorrow!

156
00:12:12,006 --> 00:12:14,308
Yeah.

157
00:12:14,331 --> 00:12:17,865
See you tomorrow!

158
00:12:17,888 --> 00:12:19,388
Scene 4: Consultation About Finding a Part-Time Job

159
00:12:19,388 --> 00:12:23,421
Daiki, hello!

160
00:12:23,444 --> 00:12:28,677
Mind if we have lunch together?

161
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:33,602
Oh, Ari! Hello!

162
00:12:33,626 --> 00:12:37,335
Of course, go ahead.

163
00:12:37,359 --> 00:12:40,226
Thank you so much!

164
00:12:40,248 --> 00:12:46,125
Actually, I have something I’d like to ask you.

165
00:12:46,149 --> 00:12:49,515
What's up?

166
00:12:49,538 --> 00:12:53,047
Is something wrong?

167
00:12:53,071 --> 00:13:01,380
Well, I’ve been thinking about looking for a new part-time job starting this fall semester.

168
00:13:01,404 --> 00:13:04,604
I see.

169
00:13:04,627 --> 00:13:09,327
Did you quit your previous part-time job?

170
00:13:09,350 --> 00:13:19,418
Yeah, I moved during summer break, and the store became too far away, so I quit.

171
00:13:19,441 --> 00:13:21,874
I see.

172
00:13:21,897 --> 00:13:26,264
What kind of part-time job are you looking for?

173
00:13:26,288 --> 00:13:32,522
I’d like a job where I can practice speaking Japanese.

174
00:13:32,546 --> 00:13:38,579
In that case, working at a café or restaurant would be great!

175
00:13:38,602 --> 00:13:43,270
How about a part-time job at an izakaya?

176
00:13:43,293 --> 00:13:47,883
I heard the hourly wage is good.

177
00:13:47,907 --> 00:13:56,464
Izakayas do pay well, but you’d have to work late into the night.

178
00:13:56,487 --> 00:14:01,754
That would be a problem if the trains stop running.

179
00:14:01,777 --> 00:14:06,010
I’d be late for my morning classes.

180
00:14:06,033 --> 00:14:09,066
Yeah, it does.

181
00:14:09,089 --> 00:14:17,687
I work at a café, and I’d recommend daytime hours.

182
00:14:17,711 --> 00:14:23,447
What kind of work do you do at Daiki’s café?

183
00:14:23,470 --> 00:14:31,304
You can practice using polite Japanese, and the work is fun too!

184
00:14:31,327 --> 00:14:36,160
Can you eat meals at the shop?

185
00:14:36,183 --> 00:14:43,572
At the café I work at, you can eat delicious meals for free!

186
00:14:43,596 --> 00:14:50,963
Since I live alone, getting free meals is really nice.

187
00:14:50,986 --> 00:14:56,253
How many days a week would you like to work, Ari?

188
00:14:56,276 --> 00:15:04,809
I also want time to study, so I’d like to work two or three days a week.

189
00:15:04,832 --> 00:15:11,499
In that case, a shop where you can easily take days off before tests would be ideal.

190
00:15:11,522 --> 00:15:17,675
Yeah, I want to study before tests.

191
00:15:17,698 --> 00:15:25,057
Actually, my café is hiring new staff right now.

192
00:15:25,081 --> 00:15:29,393
Wait, really?!

193
00:15:29,416 --> 00:15:33,950
Is the manager nice?

194
00:15:33,973 --> 00:15:39,083
He’s very kind and friendly.

195
00:15:39,106 --> 00:15:43,039
I’d love to work there!

196
00:15:43,062 --> 00:15:46,609
Could you introduce me?

197
00:15:46,632 --> 00:15:49,566
Sure thing!

198
00:15:49,589 --> 00:15:54,955
I’ll talk to the manager this evening.

199
00:15:54,978 --> 00:15:57,897
Thank you so much!

200
00:15:57,921 --> 00:16:02,454
I’ll prepare my resume.

201
00:16:02,477 --> 00:16:07,393
Okay, make sure to attach a photo too.

202
00:16:07,416 --> 00:16:12,327
Daiki, you’re so reliable.

203
00:16:12,351 --> 00:16:15,284
Thank you so much!

204
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:22,241
You’re welcome! I hope we can work together.

205
00:16:22,264 --> 00:16:23,764
Scene 5: Looking for a New Club

206
00:16:23,764 --> 00:16:29,597
Kenta, what are you looking at on the bulletin board?

207
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:33,653
Oh, Sora! Hi!

208
00:16:33,676 --> 00:16:37,753
I’m checking out the club posters.

209
00:16:37,777 --> 00:16:41,522
New clubs, huh?

210
00:16:41,545 --> 00:16:47,678
Spring was so busy I couldn’t join any.

211
00:16:47,701 --> 00:16:50,335
Yeah, it does.

212
00:16:50,358 --> 00:16:57,269
So I’ve been thinking about joining a club starting in September.

213
00:16:57,292 --> 00:17:01,077
What kind of clubs are there?

214
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:09,213
The photography club and the international exchange club are recruiting new members.

215
00:17:09,237 --> 00:17:13,370
Photography club?!

216
00:17:13,393 --> 00:17:16,660
That sounds fun!

217
00:17:16,682 --> 00:17:22,549
But I don’t have an expensive camera.

218
00:17:22,572 --> 00:17:30,123
The poster says it’s fine even if you take photos with a smartphone.

219
00:17:30,147 --> 00:17:32,904
Oh, really?!

220
00:17:32,928 --> 00:17:37,711
Then I can join too!

221
00:17:37,734 --> 00:17:41,567
What kind of activities do they do?

222
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:50,757
We go out to parks or mountains once a month to take beautiful landscape photos.

223
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:55,280
Do you also take photos of autumn foliage?

224
00:17:55,303 --> 00:17:58,470
That sounds fun!

225
00:17:58,493 --> 00:18:08,199
We’ll show the photos we take at the autumn school festival.

226
00:18:08,222 --> 00:18:11,922
I’m so happy that everyone will see my photos.

227
00:18:11,945 --> 00:18:22,379
The other international exchange circle cooks with international students and hosts events.

228
00:18:22,402 --> 00:18:27,878
That’s perfect for Kenta, who loves talking to people!

229
00:18:27,901 --> 00:18:33,008
Sora, you also love foreign cultures, right?

230
00:18:33,031 --> 00:18:35,406
Yes!

231
00:18:35,430 --> 00:18:40,332
I want to make friends with people from all over the world.

232
00:18:40,355 --> 00:18:46,093
You can visit both circles this week.

233
00:18:46,117 --> 00:18:50,390
What days can we observe them?

234
00:18:50,413 --> 00:18:57,716
The photo circle is on Wednesday, and the international exchange circle is on Thursday.

235
00:18:57,740 --> 00:19:03,850
My classes end at 4 PM on Wednesday, so I can go!

236
00:19:03,874 --> 00:19:10,376
Would you like to go together to observe the photo circle on Wednesday?

237
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:13,736
I’d love to go!

238
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:18,227
Are the seniors nice people?

239
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:23,028
Yes, the seniors are very kind.

240
00:19:23,051 --> 00:19:26,190
That puts my mind at ease.

241
00:19:26,213 --> 00:19:32,313
Would you like to go to the international exchange circle on Thursday as well?

242
00:19:32,336 --> 00:19:38,534
I can’t go on Thursday because I have a part-time job.

243
00:19:38,558 --> 00:19:41,491
Oh, I see.

244
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:44,826
No problem!

245
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:49,550
I’ll go alone on Thursday.

246
00:19:49,573 --> 00:19:54,939
Please tell me how it goes later!

247
00:19:54,962 --> 00:19:57,229
Yes!

248
00:19:57,252 --> 00:20:01,719
I’ll send you a message Thursday night!

249
00:20:01,741 --> 00:20:10,008
Let’s meet at 4:15 PM this Wednesday in front of this bulletin board.

250
00:20:10,031 --> 00:20:12,937
Got it.

251
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:17,112
I’m looking forward to Wednesday!

252
00:20:17,135 --> 00:20:19,685
Yes!

253
00:20:19,709 --> 00:20:24,652
Let’s make lots of new friends!

254
00:20:24,675 --> 00:20:26,175
Scene 6: Adjusting to Post-Summer Vacation Routine

255
00:20:26,175 --> 00:20:32,764
Nam, you’re yawning big time!

256
00:20:32,787 --> 00:20:35,973
Are you sleepy?

257
00:20:35,997 --> 00:20:44,350
Oh, Sakura. Yeah, I’m really sleepy.

258
00:20:44,374 --> 00:20:51,474
Did you stay up late last night?

259
00:20:51,497 --> 00:21:02,472
No, it’s because I stayed up late during summer vacation, so waking up in the morning is tough.

260
00:21:02,495 --> 00:21:11,811
I see. Your summer vacation sleep schedule hasn’t adjusted yet.

261
00:21:11,835 --> 00:21:20,778
Yeah. I was watching videos and playing games until 2 AM.

262
00:21:20,801 --> 00:21:25,795
That must make it hard to wake up in the morning.

263
00:21:25,819 --> 00:21:30,685
What time did you wake up this morning?

264
00:21:30,708 --> 00:21:38,475
I woke up at 8 AM and came to university without eating breakfast.

265
00:21:38,498 --> 00:21:45,766
If you don’t eat breakfast, you’ll get hungry during class.

266
00:21:45,789 --> 00:21:54,689
Yeah, I was starving during my first class.

267
00:21:54,712 --> 00:22:01,379
It’s important to wake up early in the new semester.

268
00:22:01,402 --> 00:22:07,702
How do you wake up early, Sakura?

269
00:22:07,725 --> 00:22:17,158
When I wake up, I first open the curtains to let in the morning light.

270
00:22:17,181 --> 00:22:20,976
Morning light?

271
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:31,466
Yes. Getting morning light helps me feel less sleepy and makes it easier to sleep early at night.

272
00:22:31,489 --> 00:22:34,763
That’s interesting!

273
00:22:34,787 --> 00:22:39,462
I’ll try that starting tomorrow morning.

274
00:22:39,485 --> 00:22:46,657
Also, don’t look at your phone before bed.

275
00:22:46,681 --> 00:22:53,748
I often end up scrolling on my phone in bed for too long.

276
00:22:53,771 --> 00:23:00,404
Bright screens keep you wide awake, don’t they?

277
00:23:00,427 --> 00:23:06,460
That’s why you struggle to fall asleep at night.

278
00:23:06,483 --> 00:23:10,616
Exactly.

279
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:17,473
Try sipping some warm tea and unwinding before bed.

280
00:23:17,496 --> 00:23:19,836
Got it.

281
00:23:19,859 --> 00:23:26,559
I’ll leave my phone on the desk tonight.

282
00:23:26,582 --> 00:23:34,049
Don’t push yourself—let’s gradually shift your wake-up time earlier.

283
00:23:34,072 --> 00:23:36,738
Got it!

284
00:23:36,761 --> 00:23:42,595
Oh, we have our university health checkup next week.

285
00:23:42,618 --> 00:23:45,718
Yeah, it does.

286
00:23:45,741 --> 00:23:52,841
September’s checkup is mandatory for everyone.

287
00:23:52,864 --> 00:23:59,573
Last year, there were so many people that it took forever.

288
00:23:59,596 --> 00:24:07,063
If you go early in the morning, you won’t have to wait as long.

289
00:24:07,086 --> 00:24:14,683
How about we go together next Tuesday at 9 AM?

290
00:24:14,706 --> 00:24:17,773
That sounds great!

291
00:24:17,796 --> 00:24:21,029
Let’s go together.

292
00:24:21,052 --> 00:24:26,919
It’ll be good practice for waking up early too.

293
00:24:26,942 --> 00:24:30,042
Yeah, it does.

294
00:24:30,065 --> 00:24:35,898
Let’s get back into a healthy routine and do our best!

295
00:24:35,921 --> 00:24:38,862
Got it!

296
00:24:38,885 --> 00:24:43,620
Sakura, thank you so much!

297
00:24:43,644 --> 00:24:45,144
Scene 7: University Campus Tour

298
00:24:45,144 --> 00:24:49,310
John, nice to meet you.

299
00:24:49,333 --> 00:24:53,400
I’m Mori, your tutor.

300
00:24:53,423 --> 00:24:57,323
Welcome to Japan!

301
00:24:57,346 --> 00:25:01,379
Nice to meet you, Mori.

302
00:25:01,402 --> 00:25:04,169
I’m John.

303
00:25:04,192 --> 00:25:07,625
Nice to meet you too.

304
00:25:07,648 --> 00:25:12,148
You arrived in Japan yesterday, right?

305
00:25:12,171 --> 00:25:16,484
Anything you’re having trouble with?

306
00:25:16,508 --> 00:25:19,066
Yes!

307
00:25:19,090 --> 00:25:27,123
I just got here last night, so I’m still getting familiar with the campus.

308
00:25:27,146 --> 00:25:34,781
I’ll give you a quick tour before your classes start.

309
00:25:34,805 --> 00:25:37,557
Thank you so much!

310
00:25:37,580 --> 00:25:41,613
That helps a lot.

311
00:25:41,636 --> 00:25:50,669
First, that blue building over there has the cafeteria on the first floor and the convenience store on the second.

312
00:25:50,692 --> 00:25:55,359
What time does the cafeteria open and close?

313
00:25:55,382 --> 00:26:01,861
From 8:30 AM until 7:00 PM.

314
00:26:01,884 --> 00:26:05,551
It’s affordable and delicious.

315
00:26:05,575 --> 00:26:09,453
That’s super convenient!

316
00:26:09,477 --> 00:26:13,344
I’ll eat there every day.

317
00:26:13,367 --> 00:26:20,467
The white building next to the cafeteria is the International Exchange Center.

318
00:26:20,490 --> 00:26:25,858
What can you do there?

319
00:26:25,881 --> 00:26:33,514
You can ask about visas or anything related to life in Japan.

320
00:26:33,537 --> 00:26:36,524
Got it.

321
00:26:36,548 --> 00:26:43,981
Oh, Mori, there are so many trash bins over there.

322
00:26:44,004 --> 00:26:53,720
Ah, Japanese universities have very strict trash sorting rules, so be careful.

323
00:26:53,744 --> 00:26:57,215
How do you sort it?

324
00:26:57,239 --> 00:27:06,072
Burnable trash, plastic, cans/bottles, and PET bottles—four categories.

325
00:27:06,095 --> 00:27:11,288
What do you do with PET bottles before throwing them away?

326
00:27:11,311 --> 00:27:18,945
Remove the cap and label, rinse the bottle, and then toss it.

327
00:27:18,968 --> 00:27:23,668
Got it—cap and label off.

328
00:27:23,691 --> 00:27:26,210
Understood!

329
00:27:26,233 --> 00:27:32,567
And over there is the library.

330
00:27:32,591 --> 00:27:38,425
Do you need to show your student ID to enter?

331
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:41,081
Yes!

332
00:27:41,104 --> 00:27:48,237
Just tap your student ID on the machine at the entrance.

333
00:27:48,260 --> 00:27:51,210
I see.

334
00:27:51,234 --> 00:27:56,804
I’ll keep my student ID in my bag at all times.

335
00:27:56,827 --> 00:27:59,503
Yeah, it does.

336
00:27:59,527 --> 00:28:04,960
There are plenty of quiet study seats available.

337
00:28:04,983 --> 00:28:09,097
Perfect for studying before a test!

338
00:28:09,121 --> 00:28:13,588
Is there anywhere else you'd like to know about?

339
00:28:13,611 --> 00:28:18,111
I want to use the university's Wi-Fi.

340
00:28:18,134 --> 00:28:21,034
What should we do?

341
00:28:21,057 --> 00:28:28,623
The International Exchange Center has informational flyers—let’s go together!

342
00:28:28,646 --> 00:28:31,713
Thank you so much!

343
00:28:31,736 --> 00:28:37,236
Feel free to ask me anything if you’re ever stuck.

344
00:28:37,259 --> 00:28:41,625
Let’s make the most of your university life!

345
00:28:41,648 --> 00:28:44,582
Got it!

346
00:28:44,605 --> 00:28:50,876
Mori-san, thank you so much for your kind guidance!

347
00:28:50,899 --> 00:28:52,399
Scene 8: The Appeal of Convenience Stores – Presentation

348
00:28:52,399 --> 00:28:57,066
Kim-san, you must be tired.

349
00:28:57,089 --> 00:29:03,155
Shall we start preparing for the class presentation?

350
00:29:03,178 --> 00:29:07,517
Watanabe-san, you must be tired too.

351
00:29:07,541 --> 00:29:14,208
We’re presenting in October, so we should start preparing soon.

352
00:29:14,232 --> 00:29:17,065
Yeah, it does.

353
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:22,958
The presentation time is 15 minutes, right?

354
00:29:22,982 --> 00:29:31,138
Yes! Since we’re presenting together, that’s about 7 minutes each.

355
00:29:31,162 --> 00:29:36,271
First, shouldn’t we decide on a theme?

356
00:29:36,294 --> 00:29:40,661
What would you like to talk about?

357
00:29:40,684 --> 00:29:48,351
I’d like to research Japanese convenience stores.

358
00:29:48,373 --> 00:29:52,807
Convenience stores? That sounds great!

359
00:29:52,830 --> 00:29:57,130
Why do you think convenience stores are a good topic?

360
00:29:57,153 --> 00:30:07,219
Because convenience stores in Japan are super convenient with all kinds of services—very different from my country!

361
00:30:07,242 --> 00:30:10,676
Yeah, it does.

362
00:30:10,699 --> 00:30:18,232
Japanese convenience stores really do have so many interesting services!

363
00:30:18,255 --> 00:30:24,037
Watanabe-san, what topic do you prefer?

364
00:30:24,061 --> 00:30:29,243
I think convenience stores would be great too!

365
00:30:29,267 --> 00:30:33,800
This should make for a fantastic presentation!

366
00:30:33,823 --> 00:30:36,731
I’m glad we decided on this!

367
00:30:36,755 --> 00:30:42,511
Alright, let’s go with Japanese convenience stores as our theme.

368
00:30:42,534 --> 00:30:49,970
Now that we’ve settled on a theme, shall we divide up the tasks?

369
00:30:49,993 --> 00:30:57,427
Someone can gather presentation materials, and someone else can make the slides.

370
00:30:57,450 --> 00:31:07,350
I’ll research the history and services of Japanese convenience stores using books and the internet.

371
00:31:07,373 --> 00:31:17,491
Then I’ll survey 10 international students to find out which services they use most.

372
00:31:17,514 --> 00:31:21,147
A survey? That’s a great idea!

373
00:31:21,170 --> 00:31:25,111
How will you conduct it?

374
00:31:25,135 --> 00:31:33,087
I’ll create a questionnaire on my smartphone and ask my classmates to fill it out.

375
00:31:33,110 --> 00:31:36,248
That sounds great!

376
00:31:36,272 --> 00:31:43,772
Having everyone’s input will make the presentation much clearer!

377
00:31:43,795 --> 00:31:47,533
What about the slides?

378
00:31:47,556 --> 00:31:55,513
I’ll make the slides, so Kim-san, could you create the graphs?

379
00:31:55,536 --> 00:31:58,440
Got it.

380
00:31:58,464 --> 00:32:03,164
I’ll make sure the graphs look neat!

381
00:32:03,187 --> 00:32:05,921
Thank you so much!

382
00:32:05,944 --> 00:32:11,047
When should we gather all the materials by?

383
00:32:11,071 --> 00:32:18,105
How about we summarize what we’ve found by next Friday?

384
00:32:18,128 --> 00:32:22,308
Next Friday, got it.

385
00:32:22,331 --> 00:32:25,649
Got it.

386
00:32:25,673 --> 00:32:33,225
Let’s schedule the next meeting for after class next Friday.

387
00:32:33,248 --> 00:32:35,886
Yeah.

388
00:32:35,910 --> 00:32:40,444
I’ll reserve a study room in the library.

389
00:32:40,468 --> 00:32:44,301
Thank you so much!

390
00:32:44,324 --> 00:32:51,921
Once the slides are ready, let’s practice timing them too.

391
00:32:51,945 --> 00:32:54,612
Yeah.

392
00:32:54,635 --> 00:33:00,188
Let’s work hard together so we can give a great presentation!

393
00:33:00,212 --> 00:33:04,370
Let’s do our best!

394
00:33:04,393 --> 00:33:08,393
See you next week!

395
00:33:08,416 --> 00:33:12,793
Yes! You must be tired too—good work!

396
00:33:12,817 --> 00:33:14,317
Scene 9: Preparing for the Exam Together

397
00:33:14,317 --> 00:33:17,907
Hello, Yan!

398
00:33:17,930 --> 00:33:21,968
You're studying in the self-study room today too?

399
00:33:21,992 --> 00:33:26,581
Oh, hello, Hook!

400
00:33:26,605 --> 00:33:33,786
Yeah, I'm studying for my Japanese exam in December.

401
00:33:33,809 --> 00:33:37,643
The December exam, huh?

402
00:33:37,666 --> 00:33:44,099
Actually, I'm taking a test in December too.

403
00:33:44,122 --> 00:33:47,355
Really?

404
00:33:47,378 --> 00:33:51,212
You're taking it too, Hook?

405
00:33:51,235 --> 00:33:54,801
Let’s do our best together!

406
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:57,566
Yeah.

407
00:33:57,590 --> 00:34:02,823
I’m glad I have a friend taking the same test.

408
00:34:02,846 --> 00:34:07,284
Me too.

409
00:34:07,308 --> 00:34:13,042
The three months from September are really important, aren’t they?

410
00:34:13,065 --> 00:34:15,643
Yeah, it does.

411
00:34:15,666 --> 00:34:21,837
What’s your study plan, Yan?

412
00:34:21,860 --> 00:34:29,560
First, in September, I’ll memorize words and kanji every day.

413
00:34:29,583 --> 00:34:34,549
How do you study kanji?

414
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:38,672
I’m not good at kanji.

415
00:34:38,695 --> 00:34:47,429
I use a smartphone app and practice 10 characters daily on the train.

416
00:34:47,453 --> 00:34:54,046
An app lets you study even in short bursts.

417
00:34:54,069 --> 00:34:57,736
I’ll try using it too.

418
00:34:57,759 --> 00:35:01,107
It’s great!

419
00:35:01,130 --> 00:35:06,197
What are you good at, Hook?

420
00:35:06,221 --> 00:35:15,388
I listen to Japanese radio and YouTube every day, so my listening is strong.

421
00:35:15,411 --> 00:35:18,409
That sounds great!

422
00:35:18,433 --> 00:35:28,066
I like grammar, but I struggle with reading long sentences.

423
00:35:28,089 --> 00:35:35,857
Try reading short news articles daily to improve.

424
00:35:35,881 --> 00:35:38,548
I see.

425
00:35:38,571 --> 00:35:44,117
I’ll read simple Japanese news.

426
00:35:44,140 --> 00:35:48,574
When do you start practicing with past papers?

427
00:35:48,597 --> 00:35:55,430
I’ll time myself starting from late October.

428
00:35:55,453 --> 00:36:02,210
Writing down mistakes in a notebook helps a lot.

429
00:36:02,234 --> 00:36:05,271
Got it.

430
00:36:05,295 --> 00:36:09,430
I’ll make sure to review too.

431
00:36:09,453 --> 00:36:15,920
Studying alone can be tough sometimes, right?

432
00:36:15,943 --> 00:36:18,702
Yeah, it does.

433
00:36:18,726 --> 00:36:26,426
With all the events in autumn, it might be hard to keep up.

434
00:36:26,449 --> 00:36:34,926
If you’d like, would you like to study together at the library once a week on Saturdays?

435
00:36:34,949 --> 00:36:39,449
I’d love to study together!

436
00:36:39,472 --> 00:36:43,539
We can ask each other questions.

437
00:36:43,562 --> 00:36:46,199
Yeah.

438
00:36:46,223 --> 00:36:53,693
I’ll teach you listening, so you teach me grammar!

439
00:36:53,716 --> 00:36:56,853
That sounds great!

440
00:36:56,877 --> 00:37:00,710
Let’s help each other.

441
00:37:00,733 --> 00:37:08,703
See you this Saturday at 2 PM on the second floor of the library.

442
00:37:08,726 --> 00:37:11,707
Got it.

443
00:37:11,731 --> 00:37:15,520
Saturday at 2 PM, got it.

444
00:37:15,543 --> 00:37:22,043
Let’s keep going together until December—don’t give up!

445
00:37:22,066 --> 00:37:24,639
Yeah.

446
00:37:24,662 --> 00:37:29,195
We’ll definitely pass together!

447
00:37:39,226 --> 00:37:40,726
Scene 10: Planning the School Festival Food Stall

448
00:37:40,726 --> 00:37:47,108
Sato, thank you for staying after school.

449
00:37:47,132 --> 00:37:51,284
No problem, Hana.

450
00:37:51,308 --> 00:37:57,586
Let’s discuss the plans for the school festival food stall in November.

451
00:37:57,609 --> 00:38:00,242
Yeah.

452
00:38:00,265 --> 00:38:07,699
The application form for the stall must be submitted by the end of September.

453
00:38:07,722 --> 00:38:12,088
Is it already that time?

454
00:38:12,111 --> 00:38:18,611
Has our class decided what to sell?

455
00:38:18,634 --> 00:38:26,508
Everyone in the class suggested selling foods from different countries.

456
00:38:26,532 --> 00:38:30,476
That sounds great!

457
00:38:30,499 --> 00:38:37,573
Having a variety of international dishes will make the customers happy.

458
00:38:37,597 --> 00:38:43,593
Vietnamese pho and tapioca milk tea were popular.

459
00:38:43,616 --> 00:38:50,483
Pho is warm and perfect for chilly November days.

460
00:38:50,506 --> 00:38:53,339
It sure is!

461
00:38:53,362 --> 00:39:01,196
But making the soup takes time, and I’m a little worried.

462
00:39:01,219 --> 00:39:07,725
Cooking soup outside in a tent sounds tough.

463
00:39:07,749 --> 00:39:13,227
How about bubble milk tea instead?

464
00:39:13,250 --> 00:39:25,083
We can prepare the boba tea early in the morning, so we can serve it right away.

465
00:39:25,106 --> 00:39:28,573
That way, we can serve customers quickly—great idea!

466
00:39:28,596 --> 00:39:34,168
Do we have any easy snacks to sell with it?

467
00:39:34,192 --> 00:39:39,892
What about Vietnamese sandwiches, like bánh mì?

468
00:39:39,915 --> 00:39:43,467
Bánh mì?!

469
00:39:43,490 --> 00:39:51,590
You just stuff the bread with meat and veggies—super easy to make!

470
00:39:51,613 --> 00:39:53,847
Yeah.

471
00:39:53,870 --> 00:39:59,837
And it’s packed with fresh veggies—so delicious!

472
00:39:59,861 --> 00:40:06,298
How about selling a bánh mì and bubble milk tea combo?

473
00:40:06,322 --> 00:40:10,388
A combo set? That’s a great idea!

474
00:40:10,411 --> 00:40:13,986
Yeah, that sounds perfect!

475
00:40:14,010 --> 00:40:20,344
With bread and drinks, people can eat while walking around.

476
00:40:20,368 --> 00:40:23,919
What price would work best?

477
00:40:23,942 --> 00:40:28,846
How about 500 yen for the set?

478
00:40:28,869 --> 00:40:33,147
That’s affordable and easy for everyone to buy.

479
00:40:33,171 --> 00:40:38,839
At 500 yen, everyone will happily buy it!

480
00:40:38,863 --> 00:40:43,696
Great, we’ve decided on the items and price.

481
00:40:43,719 --> 00:40:47,552
Let’s also make signs and posters.

482
00:40:47,575 --> 00:40:55,309
There’s a friend in our class who’s great at drawing—I’ll ask them to help.

483
00:40:55,332 --> 00:40:57,898
That’d be a huge help!

484
00:40:57,921 --> 00:41:04,188
Let’s also set a day to buy ingredients and prepare everything.

485
00:41:04,211 --> 00:41:12,078
How about we all make bánh mì together this Sunday?

486
00:41:12,101 --> 00:41:15,001
That sounds great!

487
00:41:15,024 --> 00:41:18,942
Whose place should we use?

488
00:41:18,965 --> 00:41:25,999
My kitchen is spacious, so let’s use my place.

489
00:41:26,022 --> 00:41:28,555
Thank you so much!

490
00:41:28,578 --> 00:41:34,845
Then, let’s meet at Hana’s place this Sunday at 11 AM.

491
00:41:34,868 --> 00:41:40,801
Yes! Let’s make some delicious bánh mì together!

492
00:41:40,824 --> 00:41:44,357
Can’t wait!

493
00:41:44,380 --> 00:41:49,447
Let’s make the school festival a fun event for everyone!